00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:16.330
Hamamatsu

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.330
Hamamatsu.

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:08.200
Located in western Shizuoka,

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:08.200
it is the largest city in the prefecture. 

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:12.910
The area around Lake Hamana to the south

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:12.910
is a resort area famous throughout Japan. 

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:16.250
It is easily accessible, and the scenery is remarkable!

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:17.700
HAMATSU, LAKE HAMANA

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.450
Also...

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.700
it's famous for its eel!

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:23.000
Umaru, I swear... I'm here for WORK.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.450
What am I going to do with her?

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:29.540
It's not like I can introduce her to Kanau...

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:31.950
This is my younger sister!

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:33.750
She sort of tagged along!

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:37.410
Just wait till it's time to review your bonus...

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.500
Huh?! No, it can't be!

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:46.700
Ah! U-um...

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:49.410
K-Kanau? Is something wrong?

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:53.950
W-well, it's about when we're supposed to be there...

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:57.660
I guess I confused 8:00 AM with 8:00 PM.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:06:59.660
Wow, what a boo-boo!

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:10.160
I-I'm sorry! I mean, if they say "8:00,"

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:10.160
you'd assume 8 AM, right?

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.700
At least we won't have to worry about being late, right?

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:16.700
She's always been the type

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:16.700
to make some huge-ass mistake...

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:23.660
Well, how about we fill the time

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:23.660
by researching the local restaurants?

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:27.660
What?! Sh-should we really break up the group

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:27.660
to do things on our own? 

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.620
There's a lot I'd like to check out, for future's sake.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.370
For future's sake...?

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:36.450
For future's sake!

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:43.950
I'd like to check out some venues

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:43.950
where we can have our ceremony, for future's sake. 

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:49.290
An excellent idea, Taihei! Yes, let's do that!

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:51.000
Uh, okay...

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.290
Score! Wanna go play pachinko?

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.080
Let's check out Hamamatsu's anime shops!

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.450
HAMAMATSU STATION

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:03.750
Big Brother! Jeez, you kept me waiting way too- Gah!

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.250
Ow, ow!

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:07.120
I can't believe you came all this way.   

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:10.450
Whatever. Let's just go.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:12.660
But after lunch, you need to leave.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:13.580
Eel time!

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:16.790
No, it's still a bit too early. 

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:20.620
How about... we do some sightseeing?

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:28.580
Note: An "anime pilgrimage" means to visit real-life locations that have

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:28.580
appeared in favorite manga or anime.

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:28.580
Oh, yeah! I wanna do an anime pilgrimage!

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:28.580
They've used a lot of places here in Hamamatsu!

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:31.950
Just make sure you don't bother the locals. 

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:35.080
Well, sure. That's just common courtesy!

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:39.870
And we'll be doing NORMAL sightseeing as well.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:42.950
Yup! Of course! 

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:47.700
Oh... the Arch of Lucky Stars!

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:52.000
This says that if two people touch it at the same time,

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:52.000
something good will happen. 

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:54.450
That sounds kinda nice...

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:02.700
Wait, wouldn't it usually be COUPLES who do this?

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:06.660
It doesn't say anywhere that siblings can't do it! 

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:11.330
And speaking of couples, Big Brother...

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:12.160
Hm?

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:16.120
Just who is... that girl who came with you?

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:18.950
She's my boss.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.120
But you call her by her first name!

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:22.950
You sure have been paying attention...

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:31.370
Note: in Japan, only people who are VERY close will call each other by

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:31.370
their first name. Even married couples often don't - they just say "you."

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:31.370
Your boss, and yet you use her FIRST name? Strange...

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:31.370
Yes, it's quite unusual. How did this come to be?

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:33.450
Why are you talking like that?

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:37.000
Bomba, Kanau, and I...

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:41.410
For better or worse, we've been pretty much inseparable,

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:41.410
and have spent a LOT of time together.  

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:44.830
Wait, she's the same age as you, but she's your boss?

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:46.790
She's actually a year younger.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:51.040
I'm not sure I should be saying this, but...

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:54.160
Kanau is the CEO's daughter. 

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:58.620
I'm sure she feels a lot of pressure

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:58.620
being section chief at her age...

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:02.410
She makes mistakes, but I think she's doing her best. 

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.790
Huh. So you're not lovers...

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:09.370
Of course not.

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:13.660
Wait, you came because

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:13.660
THAT'S what you were worried about?

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.500
No, not really. 

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:19.160
I-I came because I wanted to eat some eel!

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:21.580
Well, let's go. Let's eat already!

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:27.000
I guess you're right. It's still a little early,

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:27.000
but maybe we should get going. 

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:29.660
EEL SPIRIT

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:33.040
PLEASE IMAGINE THE AROMA OF THIS EEL.

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:37.950
Sure enough, there aren't many people here this early...

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.870
Is researching that part of your job too?

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:44.620
Sorry for the wait. Here's your order, one charbroiled eel!

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.620
Wh-whoa!

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:50.620
PLEASE IMAGINE THE AROMA OF THIS EEL.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:54.910
This isn't farm-raised eel from Lake Hamana,

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:54.910
it's wild-caught, the real deal!

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:56.250
You sure know your stuff...

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:01.040
You tasty sea creature!

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:07.250
Eel in broth is nice too.

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:08.660
Huh? Who's "E. Lynn Broth"?!

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:12.660
Look, just add soup broth and seasonings,

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:12.660
and it will really change the flavor.  

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:14.750
Kinda like rice soup, huh?

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:21.200
A rather clean flavor profile, I'd say...

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:25.450
Ah! The flavor of the wasabi

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:25.450
as it passes through the nostrils is exquisite!

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:30.160
Huh? What's with you?

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:32.830
I just...

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:36.290
I was thinking, I'm glad we came. 

00:11:36.950 --> 00:11:37.830
Yup!

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:42.040
Be careful on the way home. 

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:44.950
Okay! And you, have a safe trip!

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:46.910
Uh, I'm already here...

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:48.700
I'll be back soon.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:57.500
Do your best on the job, okay?

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:04.580
It's not even 6:00 yet,

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:04.580
so we're a bit early, but it'll be fine, right?

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.120
Okay, let's go!

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.500
Huh?

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.700
My, what cute youngsters you are! 

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:18.040
Well, you can start by prepping these potatoes. 

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:25.830
Um, we're with Diamond Service,

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:25.830
regarding data on your customer-

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:27.870
Here, you will address me as "Chef."

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:31.080
And in the kitchen, the chef's word is absolute. 

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:33.330
You will do this for me. 

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:34.870
Huh?!

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:37.500
All right, now get moving!

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:38.790
Y-yes, Chef!

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:42.290
Taihei... that outfit looks great on you!

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:42.290
You have one hour to prep 300 of these!

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:48.660
SHIZUOKA

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:48.660
TEA

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:52.750
Wait, you came because

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:52.750
THAT'S what you were worried about?

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:57.950
So sleepy... maybe I shouldn't follow him after all. 

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:11.660
I wonder why...

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:16.750
Last year - December 24th

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:22.080
If something is bothering you, just ask for advice.

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.950
Otherwise, you will regret it!

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:35.290
Today's Menu

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:35.290
Flounder Meunière

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:35.290
Lamb Confit

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:35.290
Tournedos Rossini

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:32.950
Huh? Are you hungry?

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.120
Huh?! N-no, not at all!

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:40.250
Really? Still, to think there'd

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:40.250
be a restaurant HERE of all places...

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:43.910
Oh, I know! You, me, and Umaru

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:43.910
should come here some time.

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:47.000
Food always tastes better with friends. 

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:52.290
Um, there's... 

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:54.750
something I'd like to talk to you about.

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:56.790
What is it?

00:13:56.790 --> 00:14:00.910
U-um, well... It's quite embarrassing, but...

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:03.660
um, I...

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:06.120
am looking for a particular restaurant. 

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:12.410
It's already been a week

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:12.410
since we've come to Hamamatsu. 

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.750
The staff meal's ready. It's break time. 

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:16.620
Okay. 

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:19.290
I'll take Kanau her plate.

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:26.200
Huh? Wait, has Alex always called her

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:26.200
"Kanau," by her first name?

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:28.330
Huh. I'm not sure. 

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:34.620
Whoo! Delicious as always!

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:36.290
Yes, it really is. 

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:40.660
I wasn't sure what would happen,

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:40.660
being made to work in the kitchen...

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:45.700
but being here has made it easier to write my report

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:45.700
and put together a system plan.  

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:50.290
The chef and the other staff

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:50.290
have really opened up as well... 

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:51.870
DELISH!

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:55.200
Be silent. Rather, just leave already. 

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.580
You have work to get back to in Tokyo, don't you?

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:01.750
Yeah, but doing that means going back to the grind, so...

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:05.540
Oh, my sweet Bomba. Corporate life is hard, isn't it? 

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:07.250
You've got that right!

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:11.330
Or, rather, talking to one another

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:11.330
has helped us all get along.

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:11.330
They just keep giving us more stuff to do!

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:17.790
Our CEO likes to diversify the business,

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:17.790
but it's all totally random!

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:24.410
This very restaurant started up in Tokyo, but the CEO

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:24.410
got a wild hair and, goodness! Now we're in Hamamatsu.

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:27.000
Um, I think that's enough talk about that...

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:28.830
Hey, Spiky-Haired Guy.

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:29.660
Huh?

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:31.700
You know your way around a kitchen, don't you?

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:35.040
Ah, yes. I cook at home.

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:38.040
Home, huh? Are there many of you?

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.620
No, just my younger sister. 

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:42.950
I bet she's finicky, isn't she? 

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:43.950
What?!

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:46.000
I can tell from the way you prep. 

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:49.700
The way you peel the potatoes, polish the rice...

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:52.290
all these things you do...

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:54.500
They feel like they're from cooking not for yourself,

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:54.500
but for someone else.

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:54.500
Okay, it's ready.

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:55.790
They feel like they're from cooking not for yourself,

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:55.790
but for someone else.

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:55.790
Let's eat...

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:56.660
They feel like they're from cooking not for yourself,

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:56.660
but for someone else.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.450
Big Brother!

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:02.870
Oh, my! It's not like you to speak so kindly.

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:03.910
Shut the hell up.

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:07.620
Say, why not be a lamb and work here with us?

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:08.540
Huh?

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:12.620
Yeah. You take cooking as seriously as any pro. 

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:18.500
No... I have to get back so I can do my cooking at home.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:25.160
Did I do something wrong in the game, Master?

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:28.120
No, it just felt like someone was gossiping about me...

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:32.830
Still, I'm glad to have been able

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:32.830
to learn from you, Chef.

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:34.620
Everything you've made has been delicious. 

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:37.700
He's embarrassed!

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:40.250
Ko-chan, you've got smoke coming from your ears...

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:41.450
Shut up!

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:44.660
"Ko-chan"? You mean, Chef?

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:47.290
Come to think of it, we haven't even heard his name...

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:50.700
I'm Koichiro Ebina. 

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:55.000
Ow! Ow!

00:16:55.000 --> 00:17:00.160
The same surname as our little miss Ebina, huh?

00:16:55.000 --> 00:17:00.160
Still, they don't look or act the same at all.

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:02.290
Taihei?

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:05.830
You're looking for a restaurant?

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:07.830
Yes.

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:09.950
My brother is...

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:13.410
I've heard he's working at a restaurant in Tokyo. 

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:21.910
He left home 10 years ago... still, I'm sure he's doing well.

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:26.950
All right, you all! Don't go slacking off

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:26.950
during the afternoon service!

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:28.540
Yes, Chef!

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:33.250
It couldn't be...

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:37.870
The business trip's finally over.

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:50.750
A lot has happened these past two weeks. 

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:54.750
Two weeks, and nothing happened at all!

00:17:57.500 --> 00:17:58.700
I'm home!

00:18:03.620 --> 00:18:05.250
Huh? Big Brother?

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:08.250
Oh, no! It's already been two weeks!

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.250
Rrrrrumble...

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:16.580
UMARU! I TOLD YOU NOT TO MAKE A MESS!

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:19.660
It's like you've perfected the way you get angry!

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:36.120
Sure enough, it's totally bare...

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:39.660
EEL

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:39.660
PIE

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:39.700
Oh! You brought back a lot of souvenirs, Big Brother.

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:42.080
I'm going to be giving some as gifts. 

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:44.450
I'll do it while I'm out shopping.

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:46.370
I wanna come too!

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:50.540
Th-thank you very much!

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:52.000
I hope you like it.

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:54.410
Yes! I'll treasure this forever!

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:57.290
Be sure to eat them before they expire.

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:04.160
Chef and I exchanged phone numbers...

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:04.160
maybe I should get in touch with him soon.

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.080
Something wrong, Big Brother?

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:10.200
Say, have you heard anything about Ebina's family?

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.410
Huh? Her family?

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:17.330
No, never mind. Let's just get going. 

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:22.660
Sure! But I've never been to Kirie's house,

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:22.660
so I don't know where it is.

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:24.910
Note: Shikuwasa is a form of citrus native to Okinawa.

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:24.910
Shikuwasa

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:28.200
Well, how about we just give it to her

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:28.200
next time she comes over?

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:29.120
Yeah, good idea. 

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.160
So, the next house is...

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:33.830
EEL PIE

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:33.830
Kirie! We got a souvenir gift!

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:38.330
STOP BARGING IN HERE UNINVITED!

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:44.290
How many times do I have to tell you?!

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:46.830
This is one awesome house...

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:48.750
My friend Sylphin lives here. 

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:54.950
SHPAAAAA                                AAAAN!!

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:54.950
Ah! It's Umaru, indeed!

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:58.000
You seem like you're in a good mood, Sylphin.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.580
Indeed, for my big brother has come home!

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:02.620
Oh. And who is this?

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:04.410
This is MY big brother. 

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:06.250
I'm Taihei Doma. 

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:11.330
Oh, it's that girl from before. 

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:14.450
Thank you for being such a good friend to my sister. 

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:16.870
This is a small gift from Hamamatsu. 

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:16.910
EEL PIE

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:22.200
Oh! Hm? I feel like I've just seen this...

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:22.250
EEL PIE

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:22.250
EEL PIE

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:22.250
EEL PIE

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:24.120
EEL

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:24.080
Still, thank you very much!

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:26.700
She's a bit strange, but she's nice. 

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:27.620
Yup!

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:31.330
I'm gonna go get some cola and potato chips!

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:32.660
No more than two.

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.250
Yes, I know!

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:37.910
Potatoes

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:41.410
"Not for yourself, but for someone else."

00:20:44.540 --> 00:20:46.450
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:48.370
The heck is all this?!

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:50.330
There! Take that!

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:53.660
Oh, there's the bonus!

00:20:53.660 --> 00:20:56.500
I got you now! I'm crushin' it...

00:20:57.200 --> 00:20:58.660
It's been two weeks, huh?

00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:01.540
And there's the super rare item!

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.160
Bada-bing! Woo!

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:08.450
I didn't play these much while you were gone, you know!

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:09.620
Oh, really?

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:13.290
So she was still able to have fun on her own.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.500
I guess there was no need for me to worry.

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:32.870
What's wrong?

00:21:40.830 --> 00:21:42.750
Big Brother!

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:46.700
I was... I was...

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:48.750
I was so lonely!

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:49.700
Really?

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:53.450
I was lonely and stuff!

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:54.620
Okay, I get it. 

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:56.000
Big Brother!

00:23:25.950 --> 00:23:26.790
Next Episode

00:23:25.950 --> 00:23:26.790
Preview

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:40.950
Next Episode

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:40.950
Preview

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:40.950
Episode 6: Umaru and Dreams

00:23:27.370 --> 00:23:30.330
Umaru, it's been a while since

00:23:27.370 --> 00:23:30.330
we've done the preview together, hasn't it?

00:23:30.330 --> 00:23:36.120
Ebina! Thank goodness! I'm so glad to get here and

00:23:30.330 --> 00:23:36.120
FINALLY find one of the regular female cast members! 

00:23:36.120 --> 00:23:37.750
It seems you've had it rough. 

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:40.250
Anyway, and now for the preview! Wait, we're out of time!
